  "id": "russian_kalendarnye_pesni",
  "name": "Kalendarnye pesni (Russian calendar-ritual songs)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Songs tied to the peasant agricultural year: kolyadki sung by groups going from house to house at the midwinter holidays, vesnyanki that call in the spring, songs of the Maslenitsa carnival before Lent, and Kupala songs of midsummer. Western and southern regions such as Bryansk, Belgorod and Smolensk kept many of these cycles into the 20th century; they were recorded on ethnographic expeditions issued by Melodiya and form part of the repertoire of the Dmitri Pokrovsky Ensemble.",
  "recipe": "classic modern kalendarnye pesni, field Work, Slavic balkan branch, European carnival processional. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
